    "media:imagetext": "PAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS\nBoeing 314\nBoeing built the 314 to meet a 1936 specification issued by\nPan American World Airways for a large transocean flying\nboat. First flight was in June 1938, less than 2 years after\ncontract signing. Initial\nservice was on the transatlantic\nroute, but later it saw service on Pacific routes to Hong Kong\nand New Zealand. The 314 normally carried up to /4 passen-\ngers, or 50 in a sleeper configuration. Crew was 6 to 10.\nSpecifications: wing span 152 feet, length 106 feet, gross\nweight 84.000 pounds, cruising speed 184 MPH, range\n5,200 miles.\nPublished by Aviation World, Inc., P.O. Box 188, Bethel, Conn. 06801 U.S.A.\nPhoto: Pan Amencan World Airways Collection\nNC18602\npost card\nB-054\n92142 D",
